<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Gran Canaria Guide: 11 places – Maspalomas, Roque Nublo, Mogán &amp; hidden gems – HiddenGem.Atlas</name><description>https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/gran-canaria/</description><Style id="must"><IconStyle><color>ff4cd8ff</color><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Style id="gem"><IconStyle><color>ffd0569b</color><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Placemark><name>1. Dunes of Maspalomas</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · 🆓 Free to experience · Come before sunrise and bring water. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/gran-canaria/#o1</description><Point><coordinates>-15.5829,27.74388,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Roque Nublo</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · 🆓 Free to experience · Start in the morning and take a jacket. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/gran-canaria/#o2</description><Point><coordinates>-15.6125,27.9706,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3. Puerto de Mogán</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · 🆓 Free to experience · Come in the evening for fish and stroll through the canals. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/gran-canaria/#o3</description><Point><coordinates>-15.76522,27.8174,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4. Las Palmas: Vegueta &amp; Triana</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · Start in the morning in Vegueta and end at Las Canteras beach. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/gran-canaria/#o4</description><Point><coordinates>-15.41447,28.09936,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>5. Teror &amp; Gran Canaria’s mountain villages</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · 🆓 Free to experience · Come on Sunday for the market. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/gran-canaria/#o5</description><Point><coordinates>-15.55338,28.05976,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>6. Cueva Pintada in Gáldar</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · Book the guided tour and check languages. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/gran-canaria/#o6</description><Point><coordinates>-15.65508,28.14402,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>7. Agaete, Dedo de Dios &amp; Puerto de las Nieves</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · Come for lunch and swim in the rock pools. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/gran-canaria/#o7</description><Point><coordinates>-15.71303,28.10014,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>8. Tejeda &amp; Artenara – cave houses in the mountains</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · Try almond pastries and take a jacket. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/gran-canaria/#o8</description><Point><coordinates>-15.59779,27.98153,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>9. Fataga valley &amp; Arteara</name><styleUrl>#gem</styleUrl><description>Hidden gem · Combine the valley with the Roque Nublo into a day trip. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/gran-canaria/#o9</description><Point><coordinates>-15.56384,27.8872,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>10. Playa de Amadores &amp; southern beaches</name><styleUrl>#must</styleUrl><description>Must-see · 🆓 Free to experience · Come in the morning, when it is quieter. · https://noelsprick-alt.github.io/HiddenGem.Atlas/en/guide/gran-canaria/#o10</description><Point><coordinates>-15.72383,27.78992,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Document></kml>
